verify_modes.py — array-form permission groups crash

WHAT
====
scripts/verify_modes.py:61 built a set difference over group entries:

    invalid_groups = set(groups) - ALLOWED_GROUPS

A Roo Code custom mode may declare a permission as either a plain name or the
array form [edit, {fileRegex, description}]. The array form is explicitly
declared in schemas/custom_modes.schema.json under definitions.permission
(oneOf: permissionName | ["edit", permissionOptions]) and is explicitly
handled by scripts/validate_custom_modes.py:validate_groups().

YAML list -> Python list -> unhashable, so the set construction raised
TypeError and aborted the entire verification run at the first mode that used
the documented form. The failure is a crash, not a false positive: no report
was written and no other mode was checked.

REPRODUCTION (performed at bd349c4)
===================================
1. Add custom_modes.d/<x>/<x>.yaml containing:
     groups:
       - read
       - - edit
         - fileRegex: "^docs/.*\\.md$"
           description: Documentation edits only
2. python3 scripts/validate_custom_modes.py <file>   -> exit 0 (accepted)
3. python3 scripts/verify_modes.py                   -> TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'
   at verify_mode(), line 61, called from verify_individual_files(), line 143.

WHY NO EXISTING MODE CAUGHT IT
==============================
No file under custom_modes.d/ currently uses the array form, so the shipped
tree never reaches that branch; the bug only fires for contributors following
the documented schema.

CHANGE
======
Group entries are validated individually:
  - a string entry must be a member of ALLOWED_GROUPS;
  - an array entry must be exactly ['edit', {options}] where options is a
    mapping; anything else is reported as 'malformed array-form group'.
Reporting replaces raising, so one bad mode no longer suppresses the report
for the other 300+.

VERIFICATION (performed)
========================
Fixture tree = the 305 shipped modes plus three fixtures:
  * [read, [edit, {fileRegex, description}]]  before: run aborts / after: no finding
  * [read, admin]                             before: run aborts / after: INVALID groups: ['admin']
  * [read, [edit]]                            before: run aborts / after: INVALID groups: ["malformed array-form group: ['edit']"]
The 305 shipped modes produce no group findings before or after the change
(the only new findings in the fixture run were the deliberate SHORT
roleDefinition fixtures).

RISK / ROLLBACK
===============
Single file, one function branch, no behaviour change for the shipped tree.
Revert restores the previous line exactly.
